<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Hardened-runtime entitlements for Dervo Local.app. backend/release_signing.py attaches this file when it signs the
  app with a Developer ID Application certificate (codesign, with the hardened runtime and a timestamp). Ad hoc builds
  don't use it.

  The dictionary is empty on purpose. Every entitlement here loosens the hardened runtime, so each one needs a reason
  that was checked, not guessed. What was checked on 19 Sep 2026 and why nothing is needed:

  - com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit: not needed. The web view is WKWebView, whose JavaScript runs in Apple's own
    WebContent helper process, not in dervo-local. The Rust shell runs no JIT of its own.
  - com.apple.security.cs.allow-unsigned-executable-memory and
    com.apple.security.cs.allow-dyld-environment-variables: not needed. dervo-local loads no plugins and spawns the
    Python host with a cleared environment (src/launch.rs host_command).
  - com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation: not needed. No third-party dylib or .node addon is loaded into
    dervo-local. If one is ever bundled, sign it with the same identity instead of adding this.
  - The bundled Codex runtime (Contents/Resources/runtime/codex and codex-code-mode-host) is a separate process signed
    by OpenAI with its own hardened runtime. It needs nothing from this file and isn't re-signed (codex_runtime.py
    pins its hash).
  - The Python host runs on the Python 3.13 the app carries (Contents/Resources/runtime/python, runtime/python.json)
    since beta.17, a separate process. release_signing.py signs its one Mach-O, bin/python3.13 (statically linked, no
    extension modules after trimming), with this identity and the hardened runtime and no entitlements of its own.
    Checked on 2 Oct 2026 under the hardened runtime (ad hoc): ctypes calls into Security.framework, CoreFoundation,
    libSystem and libproc, pty.fork, fcntl, os.killpg, sqlite3 and ssl with /etc/ssl/cert.pem all work, and nothing in
    the backend uses ctypes callbacks, so no allow-unsigned-executable-memory. Spawning it needs no entitlement here.
    Up to beta.16.4 the host was /Library/Frameworks/Python.framework, signed by the Python Software Foundation.
  - com.apple.security.network.client and the other App Sandbox keys: not needed. Dervo isn't sandboxed.
  - keychain-access-groups: not yet. The Keychain fix in notes/devid-plan.md uses the login Keychain's default
    access (trusts the signed app by its designated requirement), which needs no entitlement. Add this key only if
    that plan moves to the data-protection keychain.

  If a signed build fails where an ad hoc build worked, the crash report names the missing entitlement. Add it here
  with the reason, one line each.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
</dict>
</plist>
